++
++C03: the App judges the trailing question that names the volume the person asked about apart from an invented level, and «no toques» is a prohibition (AUDIO1579)
++
++AUDIO1577 measured that «subí el volumen y decime qué fecha es» and both variants read the clock and the mind's first draft was already the intended final («Hoy es 15 de septiembre de 2026. ¿Cuánto querías aumentar el volumen?»), while `UserMessagePolicy.InventedVolume` rejected every final that mentions the volume when the observed facts carry no level. When the person's own request names the volume, the rule now judges only the sentences before the trailing question (`WithoutTrailingQuestion`): the question states no level, it asks for one. The boundary «No toques el volumen.» answered with a question because `_negative_action_forms` did not know «toques»; «toca»/«touch» now count as prohibited actions, as «usa» already did.
++
++Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
